# Runtime state and logs live on the device, not in the repo.
device/state/
device/log/

# Locally rendered previews of the lock screen are build artefacts.
preview/*.png

# artwork/ is its OWN git repository (published as kindle-screensaver), so it is
# excluded here. Committing it would record a bare gitlink and the archive would
# contain an empty directory -- and the device updater would then think it had
# fetched artwork it never got. The frames are fetched from the art repo by
# ART_URL instead, which is a separate mechanism with its own config.
#
# manifest.json and preview.png inside artwork/ ARE part of the format, so they
# must stay committed *there*.
artwork/

# weather/ is its OWN git repository too, for the same reason: it is a
# self-contained shell library that knows nothing about e-ink, clocks or layout,
# and it is published separately. Committing it here would record a bare gitlink
# and the archive would contain an empty directory.
#
# This repo consumes it as a VENDORED COPY at device/lib/weather.sh, which IS
# committed here because it is part of the device payload. tools/sync-weather.ps1
# refreshes that copy and verify.ps1 fails if the two ever drift apart.
weather/

# Scratch output from tools/make-animation.ps1 before it is meant to be committed.
*_tmp/
*.tmp

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
